+# Harrow High is a container in `tallis` until Phase 3, then a zone of its own (repository owner's decision, 2026-10-06)
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Decision | **"(A) Container, zone from Ph3 (Recommended)".** In Phases 1 and 2 Harrow High is an object container in zone `tallis`, as 02 §5.5 says. From Phase 3 it is its own single-cell zone, `harrow-high`, with its own server cell, and `tallis` keeps the orbit and the Saltmarch container |
+| Decided by | The repository owner (the user), on 2026-10-06, in answer to the Director's question of 14:27 UTC (the first ask, of 14:24 UTC, got the answer "explain this with more detail and re-ask me") |
+| Recorded by | The Director (Claude Code agent), on 2026-10-08, as part of plan revision 15 (09 §5.10.2 D1; `CONSISTENCY.md` §43; PR #67) |
+| Files | Phase 1 and 2: Harrow High's spatial documents sit in zone `tallis`'s folder, `content/zones/tallis/`, as a container (02 §5.6). Phase 3: they move to `content/zones/harrow-high/` |
+| Editing session | `zone-tallis` for the container (07 §1.8.2); from Phase 3, `zone-harrow-high` for the zone |
+| Rework | None in the tree (below). The cost the owner accepted is Phase 3 work: a content move, and docking and undocking as a zone transition |
+
+## The question and the answer
+
+The Director (the orchestrating agent, 09 §5.1) asked the owner twice on 2026-10-06. Both questions and the
+answers below are quoted as the question tool returned them; only the owner's words are the decision.
+
+**First ask (14:24 UTC).** The question:
+
+> Harrow High: 02 §5.5 keeps the station interior a container in zone 'tallis' (Phase 1). ED-20, NS-3.11 and
+> NS-4.6 treat Harrow High as its own single-cell zone. Which should the plan say?
+
+The owner's answer, verbatim:
+
+> explain this with more detail and re-ask me
+
+**Re-ask (14:27 UTC).** The question:
+
+> Harrow High is the orbital station over planet Harrow. Its concourse is BENCH-1: 200 avatars, 60 NPCs, 40
+> screens. M1 'Descent' starts with undocking a Kestrel from it.
+>
+> Today the plan describes it two ways:
+> • As a container (02 §5.5, Phase 1). Tallis space and Harrow's surface are one zone, `tallis`, run by one
+> cell. The station interior is an object container inside it, like Saltmarch. That is what makes the
+> orbit-to-interior descent (BENCH-2) seamless: there is no server handoff in Phase 1.
+> • As a zone of its own, in three later criteria. ED-20 (Ph3, editor collaboration) runs "a second zone
+> session (Harrow High)"; a zone session exists only for a zone. NS-3.11 (Ph3, live server migration)
+> migrates "a 500-bot, 20k-entity single-cell hub (Harrow High)" 100 times. NS-4.6 (Ph4, crash recovery)
+> kills the cell of "single-cell Harrow High" 10 times under 500 bots.
+>
+> The question: does the hub get its own zone (and server cell) once the engine can hand players between
+> zones (Ph2–3), or does it stay a container in `tallis` forever? Making it a zone from Phase 1 isn't viable:
+> zone handoff doesn't exist until Phase 2, so M1's undock would break.
+
+The owner selected **"(A) Container, zone from Ph3 (Recommended)"**. The option's description, as the owner
+saw it:
+
+> Phase 1 is unchanged. From Phase 3 the station is its own single-cell zone, so the densest social space
+> gets a dedicated server and scales on its own, and the three criteria stand as written. Cost: in Phase 3
+> its files move to their own zone folder, and docking or undocking becomes a zone transition (the client
+> prefetches the destination; the handoff hitch budget applies).
+
+and its preview:
+
+```
+Ph1-2:  zone `tallis` = space + Harrow surface
+          ├─ container: Harrow High interior
+          └─ container: Saltmarch
+Ph3+:   zone `tallis`      (orbit, 4 cells in NS-3.11/4.6)
+          └─ container: Saltmarch
+        zone `harrow-high` (1 cell, the hub)
+
+ED-20, NS-3.11 (a), NS-4.6 (b): unchanged
+02 §5.5: + "Harrow High becomes its own zone in Ph3"
+WP impact: a Ph3 content move + dock = zone transition
+```
+
+The owner then wrote: "You can now continue with these answers in mind." The other option or options the
+question offered are not quoted here: the Director kept the text of the chosen one only. The Director's
+description of PR #67 had stated the alternative as: Harrow High stays a container, and ED-20, NS-3.11 and
+NS-4.6 name another single-cell hub zone (thresholds unchanged).
+
+## Why the question came up
+
+At plan revision 14 the plan described Harrow High two ways, as the question says.
+
+- **As a container in zone `tallis`:** 02 §5.5's Phase 1 layout ("the station interior is a container.
+  BENCH-2 is therefore seamless without a handoff"), and 07 §2.1's T01 MVP, "one zone with its frame hierarchy
+  (Tallis → Harrow → Saltmarch)".
+- **As a zone:** ED-20 (07 §5.2, Phase 3: "a second zone session (Harrow High, 6 collab-bots)"), NS-3.11 (a)
+  (04 §11.4: "a 500-bot, 20k-entity single-cell hub (Harrow High)") and NS-4.6 (b) ("single-cell Harrow High").
+
+The two readings differ by phase, and the decision keeps both texts as written by dating the change: a
+container in Phases 1 and 2, a zone from Phase 3.
+
+## What changed in the plan (revision 15)
+
+- **02 §5.5.** The Phase 1 layout names Harrow High as the container, and a new bullet, "Harrow High becomes
+  its own zone in Phase 3", records the decision, the zone id (`harrow-high`) and session
+  (`zone-harrow-high`, 07 §1.8.2), what `tallis` keeps (the orbit, four cells in NS-3.11 and NS-4.6, and the
+  Saltmarch container), and the two costs below. The same section's zone-session wording is dated: designers
+  open the zone in the editor (T01) and, from Ph3, edit it in its session (07 §1.8.2 lists the zone session as
+  Ph3), which resolves the "(from Ph3, 07 §1.8)" wording note that the review of PR #51 left open.
+- **ED-20, NS-3.11 (a) and NS-4.6 (b).** Unchanged, as the option says: they refer to the Phase 3+ hub (ED-20's
+  second zone session, NS-3.11's single-cell hub) and the Phase 4 hub (NS-4.6 (b)).
+- **09 §2.** WP-1.22 (Phase 1 content) builds Harrow High as a container in `tallis`; WP-3.9 (Phase 3 content)
+  moves its files to `content/zones/harrow-high/` and makes it a zone (D3: unstarted WPs' rows are edited in
+  the plan PR).
+
+## The work-package impact
+
+- **The Phase 3 content move.** WP-3.9 (CT, depends on 3.1–3.7) moves Harrow High's documents from
+  `content/zones/tallis/` to `content/zones/harrow-high/` (T28's `collab.scope` rule, 07 §1.8.2, requires every
+  spatial document to sit under its zone's folder). As for any zone, the new zone also needs its
+  `ZonePartitionDef` (02 §5.5: `Whole`, one region, for a single-cell zone) and its session.
+- **Docking and undocking become a zone transition.** 04 §7 lists docking among the zone transitions, which
+  are gateway route changes, not reconnects: the client gets `ZoneChange` and "streams destination containers
+  during transit VFX (prefetch starts at spool)", and 02 §5.5 says the client "keeps a second view that
+  prefetches the destination". The plan's criteria for a zone transition apply as written: 04 §7's target
+  and **NS-1.4** (≤ 3 s, 0 reconnects; owner WP-1.11, "handoff-seam zone transfer"), **CL-4** (08: p99 ≤ 3 s, no
+  frame > 50 ms in world), and **AAA-SRV-5** (01 §3: "Zone transition / handoff p99", ≤ 3 s in Ph1 and Ph2,
+  < 100 ms in Ph3 and Ph4, < 50 ms in Ph5; owner WP-3.1 for Ph3). This record adds no budget and moves none.
+  Which of those values a dock or undock must meet in Phase 3 is not decided here; the criteria say what they
+  say, and the owners above show it.
+
+## Code and content
+
+- No code or content places Harrow High yet. The repository's `content/zones/` holds `tallis` with the
+  Saltmarch container only (`saltmarch.hcont` and one `.hent`), and `git grep` outside `docs/` and
+  `third_party/` for "Harrow High" finds two files: the IP-name policy (`tools/lint/ip_names_policy.cmake`) and
+  a lint fixture (`tools/lint/tests/ip_names/clean/content/records/ships.jsonc`). Neither depends on whether
+  Harrow High is a container or a zone.
+- `helios-cell` and `helios-gateway`'s defaults call the zone `tallis` (`--zone tallis`, `--default-zone
+  tallis`), which matches Phases 1 and 2 and does not change.
+- No schema, registry, threshold or workflow changes, and no rework WP: the plan's own Phase 3 rows
+  carry the work.
