, manifest read and write ≤ 400 ms (≤ 800 ms for the deepest paths with their collision keys in random order); the trust chain runs once per launch (0.34 ms C++, 0.17–0.24 ms Go) and has no budget. Fuzzing (2026-10-05): `patch_fuzz_trust_parser` under Clang ASan/UBSan ran 7.3 M inputs in 11 minutes (1,704 edges, no finding); Go's `FuzzParseKeyset`, `FuzzParsePointer` and `FuzzVerifyManifestHeader` ran 2.4 M, 1.5 M and 1.4 M inputs in 5 minutes each, no failure; after review round 1, with `-max_len=70000`, 5.6 M inputs in 10.5 minutes (1,769 edges) plus 1.7 M in 3 minutes with `-len_control=0` (inputs up to 65,708 bytes), and Go 2.1 M, 2.1 M (two runs) and 0.1 M, no finding. **Nightly P0 (WP-0.16):** `TestPerfDeepPaths` (`services/pkg/manifest`), a 2× ratio of deep-path to shallow-path read time, failed on the 2026-10-05 nightly's `windows-go` job (37297423497: 2.8×), on CI's Linux Go job for #63 (2.0×, passed on re-run) and on CI's Windows Go job for `main` at fb9517f (run 37416153106: 2.0×); the 2× stands, and a WP-0.16 follow-up finds why deep paths read slower on those runners |
